ex:G1 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "Every contradictory maintenance, fault or mileage record is listed with the rule it breaks within a week of being entered"@en ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope ; backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Mission ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:A2 ; backlog:hasGoalRationale "this is the change the maintenance unit asked for: errors found when made, not when a maintenance is missed" .
ex:G2 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "The graph holds every vehicle, reading, fault and visit of the export, with each fault typed from the scheme"@en ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope ; backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Scope ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:A1 ; backlog:hasGoalRationale "a record missing from the graph is a record no rule can check" .
ex:G3 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "The supervisor sees which vehicles are due for periodic maintenance and the monthly violation trend without a developer"@en ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope ; backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Scope ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:A3 ; backlog:hasGoalRationale "the panel is what turns a report into a weekly habit of the unit" .
ex:G4 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "The tool never writes to the Portal and no personal data enters the graph, the reports or the repository"@en ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope ; backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Containment ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:A2 ; backlog:hasGoalRationale "the Portal is live and the KVKK regime applies; the checker must stay a reader" .
ex:Spec a backlog:Specification ; backlog:hasSpecificationText "The system reads the vehicle, maintenance, fault and mileage-history exports of the Portal as Excel or CSV files, replaces plates and names with codes, and builds an RDF graph of vehicles, mileage readings, fault records and maintenance visits, with fault types taken from a SKOS scheme. It validates the graph against a SHACL rule set in which each rule has a severity: mileage going backwards, a fault mileage above the vehicle's current mileage, a repair dated before its fault, a missing fault type and a periodic maintenance mileage that has been passed without a visit. It writes a report that names each violating record, the rule, the severity and the contradicting values, writes a correction-proposal file for the clerk, and records the run in PROV-O with the export's hash and the rule-set version. It computes each vehicle's average daily mileage from the history and forecasts the date its periodic maintenance falls due. A web panel shows violations per vehicle, the monthly trend and the vehicles due within a chosen number of days. When an export is missing a table or a required column, the tool stops and names the missing part instead of checking a partial graph." .
ex:Scen1 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Nominal ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given an export in which vehicle A017 has a mileage reading of 84,300 followed by a fault recorded at 83,900, when the clerk runs the check, then the report lists the fault record under the rule 'mileage may not go backwards' with both values" .
ex:Scen2 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Rejection ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given an export in which the mileage-history table is missing, when the clerk runs the check, then the tool produces no report and says which table is missing" .
ex:Scen3 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Boundary ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given a vehicle whose periodic maintenance mileage equals its current mileage exactly, when the check runs, then the vehicle appears as due today and not as overdue" .
ex:Scen4 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Absent ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given a vehicle with no mileage reading at all, when the check runs, then the forecast for that vehicle says 'no history' instead of a date" .
ex:O1 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Contradictory records found within a week of entry"@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G1 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Derived ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "violations found by the weekly run divided by the corrections the unit made in the same month, from the report files and the unit's correction list" ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "49 contradictory fault records in September 2026, found only when noticed" ; backlog:hasTargetValue "100% of them found by the weekly run" ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Increase .
ex:O2 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Records of the export present in the graph"@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G2 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Counted ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "rows in the four export tables compared with the subjects of the matching type in the graph, by a SPARQL count after each import" ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "0% (no graph today)" ; backlog:hasTargetValue "100%" ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Increase .
ex:O3 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Hours a developer spends reading the database to find record errors"@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G1 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Judged ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "hours per month recorded by the developer for manual correction work, before and after the tool" ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "5 hours a month" ; backlog:hasTargetValue "1 hour a month" ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Decrease .
ex:O4 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Vehicles whose periodic maintenance is passed without a visit"@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G3 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Counted ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "vehicles in the monthly report whose current mileage exceeds their periodic maintenance mileage with no visit recorded" ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "45 vehicles on 17 October 2026" ; backlog:hasTargetValue "0" ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Decrease .
ex:O5 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Personal data items and Portal writes"@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G4 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Counted ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "a regex scan of the repository, the graph and the reports for plates, names and identity numbers, and the absence of any database write statement in the code" ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "0" ; backlog:hasTargetValue "0" ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Hold .
ex:Model_Activity a backlog:ModelArtifact ; backlog:hasModelKind backlog:Kind_ActivityDiagram ; backlog:hasModelLevel backlog:Level_Analysis ; backlog:declaresState "The clerk exports the four tables from the Portal and uploads them. The importer checks that every table and required column is present; if one is missing it stops and names it. Otherwise it anonymises plates and names, builds the graph and loads it into the store. The validator runs the SHACL rules; each violation is collected with its severity. The reporter writes the HTML and CSV report and the correction proposal, and records the run in PROV-O. The forecaster computes each vehicle's daily mileage rate and its due date. The panel reads the latest run and shows the summary; the clerk corrects the named records in the Portal and the next weekly run shows whether the violations are gone." .
ex:Model_Sequence a backlog:ModelArtifact ; backlog:hasModelKind backlog:Kind_SequenceDiagram ; backlog:hasModelLevel backlog:Level_Analysis ; backlog:declaresState "The clerk sends the export files to the command-line tool. The tool asks the importer to parse and anonymise them and receives a graph. It sends the graph to the Oxigraph store, then asks pySHACL to validate the graph against the rule set and receives a validation report. It passes the report to the reporter, which queries the store with SPARQL for the contradicting values and writes the files. The reporter asks the provenance recorder to store the run. The panel, when opened by the supervisor, queries the store for the latest run, the per-vehicle counts and the forecast, and renders the page." .
ex:Model_Class a backlog:ModelArtifact ; backlog:hasModelKind backlog:Kind_ClassDiagram ; backlog:hasModelLevel backlog:Level_Analysis ; backlog:declaresState "Vehicle has a code, a current mileage, a periodic maintenance mileage and many MileageReadings, FaultRecords and MaintenanceVisits. MileageReading has a date and a value. FaultRecord has a date, a mileage and a FaultType from the SKOS scheme. MaintenanceVisit has a date, a mileage, a kind (periodic or corrective) and an optional repaired FaultRecord. Rule has an identifier, a text, a severity and a SHACL shape. Violation links one record to one Rule with the contradicting values. CheckRun has a date, the export hash, the rule-set version and many Violations; it is a PROV-O activity that used the export and generated the report. Forecast belongs to a Vehicle and has a daily rate and a due date." .
